WEBVTT

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:07.220
The original Creation was destroyed by the 
evil gods that it had brought into existence.

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:11.230
Thus began the age of war among the gods.

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:14.950
The big statues in the temple 
are the virtuous gods, right?

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:18.020
To a human, yes, they would be.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:19.520
What does that mean?

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.150
Among the legends told since ancient times

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:25.110
is a battle between the lightning god Volt,

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:27.480
the king of the gods who 
governs order and judgment,

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:30.340
and his elder brother, the war god Iltreat.

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:33.030
The elder brother had the 
advantage in the beginning,

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:36.620
but Volt, with the divine protection 
of his wife, the earth-mother Mater,

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:39.770
banished the war god to 
the depths of the earth.

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:45.150
The war god continues to lurk within the 
earth, vigilantly plotting his revenge.

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:49.280
There are other similar stories, 
but they all take the same general shape.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:50.830
What are your thoughts?

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:53.280
Isn't it just a fable?

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:54.370
Oh?

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:58.870
Ruling in this world starts 
with violence and despotism,

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:00.870
but eventually, 
agriculture starts to thrive,

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:02.680
and law and order begin to reach everyone.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:07.620
But over time, that also leads to violent 
overthrows... Something like that.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:10.620
You are very sharp indeed.

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:15.330
Volt, the god of order and 
judgment, is a virtuous god.

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:17.850
The war god, on the other hand, 
is considered an evil god.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:22.070
But if that order becomes corrupt, 
Volt could become an evil god,

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:26.360
and by defeating that corruption, 
Iltreat could become a virtuous god.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:29.880
In short, the concept of 
virtuous gods and evil gods

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:33.810
is a distinction applied by those 
who place their faith in them.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:38.040
The priests would not be pleased 
with me for saying so, however.

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:40.460
Naturally, you must not 
speak of this to Mary.

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:41.960
I won't.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:47.200
Besides, the gods think about things 
based on different standards than ours.

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:51.130
It is impossible for one with a 
human's sense of good and evil

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:52.700
to gauge their true intentions.

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:55.310
You know, Gus, you're pretty rock 'n roll.

00:01:55.310 --> 00:01:56.830
What on earth does that mean?

00:01:56.830 --> 00:01:57.510
Er...

00:01:57.510 --> 00:02:00.470
It means, like... you don't fit in any mold!

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:03.980
Children truly make up some 
bizarre words sometimes...

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:06.450
But I do like the sound of that.

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:17.150
The Faraway Paladin

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:44.540
<i>Becoming free from obstructive thoughts 
doesn't mean thinking about nothing.</i>

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:47.260
<i>You just block out the past and future,</i>

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:49.350
<i>and focus only on the present.</i>

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:54.660
<i>I need to offer all of my current 
insignificant self to the gods,</i>

00:03:55.350 --> 00:03:57.770
<i>and then dive in deep.</i>

00:03:58.220 --> 00:03:59.270
<i>As far as I can.</i>

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:11.770
This concludes the five-day Silent Prayer.

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:13.340
You did very well.

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:17.650
<i>I've done nothing but pray continuously 
for the past five days.</i>

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:21.190
Do you feel all right physically, Will?

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:22.690
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:25.660
And you're only thirteen. 
How remarkable you are.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:28.440
Only because I've been praying 
with you all these years.

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:35.540
<i>It's been five years since 
my arms were burned.</i>

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:39.270
<i>Mary says she could heal the 
scars with her blessing,</i>

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:41.310
<i>but I chose to keep them.</i>

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:44.350
<i>Blood said they were my badge 
of manhood, after all.</i>

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:47.740
I'll prepare all of your favorite 
things for dinner tonight.

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:48.910
Yay!

00:04:50.170 --> 00:04:52.750
Memorize all of this by tomorrow.

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:53.860
Huh?!

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:56.920
<i>Gus's lessons became more difficult,</i>

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:58.710
<i>and there was a lot more to keep track of,</i>

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:02.160
<i>but I stuck to it for all I was worth.</i>

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:06.000
<i>And then his lessons became 
even more intensive.</i>

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:10.120
<i>It's as if he wants me 
to get fed up and quit.</i>

00:05:11.230 --> 00:05:15.130
<i>Still, Mary and Gus were 
nothing compared to...</i>

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:17.070
All right!

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:19.460
Let's move on to our main event of the day.

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:22.220
What is that?

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:25.290
Your opponent. I caught him in the ruins.

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:27.220
Uh, that's not what I mean!

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:30.720
What's the problem? 
It's just a low-ranked demon's corpse.

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:33.190
<i>Demons can become undead, too?</i>

00:05:33.190 --> 00:05:34.260
Okay, go.

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:34.920
Wait a—

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:43.940
<i>I got him!</i>

00:05:45.890 --> 00:05:47.610
Blood, I win!

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:49.980
Y-Yeah... Good job.

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:51.660
So this is what they mean

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:54.820
when they say a trained warrior 
can kill with mechanical reflexes!

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:56.580
Y-Yeah, I guess so...

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:58.570
Blood?

00:05:59.650 --> 00:06:02.370
Well, for your first killing 
match, that wasn't bad.

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:04.670
Hear me? It just <i>wasn't bad</i>!

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:05.950
Don't get a big head!

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:07.640
Oh, that's what you meant?

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:10.920
Well? I'm a genius, right?

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:13.370
You might just be a genius...

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:15.630
C'mon, aren't you gonna 
chew me out for that?

00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:16.460
Okay!

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:19.980
Why don't we speed things up and 
try something harder, genius?

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:20.860
Huh?

00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:27.050
<i>The ruined city that I always 
saw from the top of the hill.</i>

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:30.180
<i>That day was the first 
time I set foot in it.</i>

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:41.500
I didn't know there were passages 
like this underground.

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:44.650
Humans and dwarfs used to live here.

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:47.100
Their blacksmith helped me out a lot.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:52.550
But now it's just a danger zone filled 
with mindless, wandering undead.

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:56.050
That's why we never allowed 
you to enter here before.

00:06:57.010 --> 00:06:58.430
This spot should be good.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:00.880
You've got all your stuff, right?

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:01.570
Yeah.

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:04.810
My sword, shield, bread, 
jerky, and a waterskin.

00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:07.270
Those things are everything 
to you right now.

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:09.290
Okay. Now escape from here.

00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:09.730
Huh?

00:07:09.980 --> 00:07:12.730
I'll be waiting outside. Don't die, now.

00:07:12.730 --> 00:07:14.680
W-Wait a minute! Blood!

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:18.050
<i>H-He can't be serious!</i>

00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:19.220
Lumen!

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:18.870
Light

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:21.660
Blood?

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:25.280
The exit is this way, right?

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:29.350
But what was it Blood said a minute ago?

00:07:29.350 --> 00:07:30.620
This place is...

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:36.250
Of course.

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:48.950
<i>I'm pretty sure Blood is testing 
my overall practical ability.</i>

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:53.980
I didn't know being alone was such 
a lonely, anxious feeling...

00:07:55.990 --> 00:07:58.400
<i>I had forgotten even that fact.</i>

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:00.640
<i>Even though I spent all of 
my previous life alone...</i>

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:05.890
Ever since I came here, 
Blood and Mary have been by my side.

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:09.770
<i>In this world, people reach 
adulthood at fifteen,</i>

00:08:09.770 --> 00:08:11.690
<i>so I'll be striking out on my own soon.</i>

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:16.570
<i>That's probably part of why all of their 
lessons have gotten so much harder.</i>

00:08:16.570 --> 00:08:17.650
<i>In that case...</i>

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:20.480
I want to give back the best results I can.

00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:25.670
I want them to boast that I was a pupil 
worth teaching, that they're proud of me.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:37.570
<i>That's probably an undead Vraskus demon.</i>

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:41.880
<i>They can use the Words. They're stronger 
than any opponent I've faced.</i>

00:08:42.530 --> 00:08:46.020
<i>Should I stay hidden and slip 
past it? Go another route?</i>

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:49.050
<i>What would Blood do?</i>

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:12.370
<i>It's strong, but not as strong as Blood!</i>

00:09:15.230 --> 00:09:16.950
Tacere, Os!

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:16.410
Be Silent, Mouth

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:36.050
Oh, no... This is not the place 
to be stuck without a weapon...

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:45.160
This isn't a demon weapon.

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:47.510
A dwarven magic spear?

00:09:48.470 --> 00:09:50.180
It's better than nothing.

00:09:56.800 --> 00:09:59.040
There's a draft here.

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:00.710
Maybe I'm near the exit.

00:10:01.340 --> 00:10:04.190
I wonder how long this 
place has been deserted.

00:10:04.190 --> 00:10:07.000
It sounded like Blood knew 
it while it was populated...

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:10.580
Does that mean the three of them 
became undead around the same time?

00:10:11.120 --> 00:10:14.600
From the level of degradation, 
it's been more than just a decade or two.

00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:19.680
<i>I already know there are no humans 
living anywhere near here.</i>

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:23.120
<i>I wonder where my birth parents are...</i>

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:26.900
<i>And why am I in these ruins?</i>

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:29.630
<i>My real parents...</i>

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:43.370
Episode 2
The Wandering Sage

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:45.300
Gus?

00:10:47.410 --> 00:10:48.990
You're Gus, right?

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:54.640
Why aren't you saying anything? And...

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:58.030
<i>Why are you glaring at me like that?</i>

00:10:58.510 --> 00:11:00.850
Did Blood tell you I was here?

00:11:02.020 --> 00:11:05.390
Or is this another lesson of some kind?

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:07.780
It's a lesson, right? With conditions for—

00:11:07.780 --> 00:11:10.180
Expergisci!

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:09.640
Awaken

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:15.800
A golem?!

00:11:20.350 --> 00:11:21.060
Gus!

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:25.240
<i>He's serious!</i>

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:28.090
<i>I'm aiming for...</i>

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:42.430
Stone Blast can carry that much force?!

00:11:45.340 --> 00:11:47.210
Cadere Araneum!

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:46.220
Falling

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:47.220
Spiderweb

00:11:47.210 --> 00:11:48.440
Mendacium!

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:48.220
It Is False

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:54.590
<i>Grease magic?</i>

00:11:54.590 --> 00:11:55.900
<i>When did...</i>

00:11:57.200 --> 00:11:59.900
<i>His magic projection is way too quick!</i>

00:11:59.900 --> 00:12:01.110
<i>A double cast?!</i>

00:12:01.110 --> 00:12:02.060
Robigus!

00:12:01.110 --> 00:12:02.070
Slow

00:12:02.060 --> 00:12:03.200
Mendacium!

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:02.950
It Is False

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:03.910
Somnus!

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:03.910
Sleep

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:05.120
Mendacium!

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:04.740
It Is False

00:12:05.460 --> 00:12:07.840
<i>Why? Why, Gus?</i>

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:09.910
Expergisci!

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:09.910
Awaken

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:11.650
<i>A triple cast?!</i>

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:15.700
<i>I'm gonna be killed by one of my own 
parents, and I don't even know why...</i>

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:18.460
<i>This can't be real!</i>

00:12:20.660 --> 00:12:22.690
<i>No... No!</i>

00:12:22.690 --> 00:12:24.410
<i>No! No! No!</i>

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:27.180
<i>I don't want that! I don't want to die!</i>

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:27.890
<i>What can I...</i>

00:12:28.050 --> 00:12:31.600
<i>Oh, right! This spear should
work on a ghost like Gus!</i>

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:34.900
<i>He's the one who tried to kill me first.</i>

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:38.640
<i>No one can complain if I kill him!</i>

00:12:39.740 --> 00:12:40.450
<i>Pierce!</i>

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:42.000
<i>Pierce!</i>

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:43.240
<i>Pierce him!</i>

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:44.260
<i>Kill him!</i>

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:54.420
Tell me, Gus...

00:12:55.860 --> 00:12:57.030
Grandpa...

00:12:58.690 --> 00:13:01.420
If you really have to kill me...

00:13:02.100 --> 00:13:05.260
There must be some reason you're 
being forced to do it, right?

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:12.550
I know you wouldn't do this 
if you didn't have a reason.

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:13.830
I know that.

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:18.320
<i>If Gus was really serious, he wouldn't 
need to play around like this.</i>

00:13:18.680 --> 00:13:21.070
<i>If he throws around a lot of fire magic,</i>

00:13:21.070 --> 00:13:23.290
<i>I'll die of oxygen deficiency and toxicity.</i>

00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:25.130
<i>If he makes the ceiling collapse,</i>

00:13:25.130 --> 00:13:28.970
<i>his ghost body won't be hurt, 
but I'll be crushed and die.</i>

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:32.870
I know... I know that, but...

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:37.920
I still don't want to fight you to the death.

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:43.270
Hurting you would make me feel 
worse than dying myself.

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:49.840
If that's really important 
to you, that's fine.

00:13:51.130 --> 00:13:53.770
You can kill me.

00:13:54.950 --> 00:13:57.010
I'm not afraid.

00:13:57.560 --> 00:13:59.730
I'm your pupil.

00:14:01.160 --> 00:14:05.820
B-But... I'd appreciate it if you 
didn't make it hurt too much...

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:07.230
Ah, forgive me!

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:10.250
I took that a bit too far for a lesson!

00:14:10.480 --> 00:14:13.200
This place did give me an 
advantage, but still, I win.

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:15.590
Yes, I'm sure that was a shock to you,

00:14:15.590 --> 00:14:19.130
but now you've gained experience in 
combat against a sorcerer! Right?

00:14:15.820 --> 00:14:19.130
<i>What shocks me isn't that this was a lesson.</i>

00:14:19.490 --> 00:14:20.380
Gus...

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:21.990
Now, don't ask questions!

00:14:21.990 --> 00:14:24.930
If you managed to defeat a 
Vraskus and take his spear,

00:14:24.930 --> 00:14:27.480
even Blood will congratulate you heartily!

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:31.210
Oh, yes! Weren't the double 
and triple casts amazing?

00:14:28.150 --> 00:14:33.720
<i>It's that Gus is trying to pass 
all of this off as a lesson.</i>

00:14:31.210 --> 00:14:35.460
I'll teach you some ill-mannered 
tricks like that soon!

00:14:35.460 --> 00:14:36.350
So...

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:38.810
Please don't be upset.

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:40.660
Come, Will.

00:14:40.660 --> 00:14:44.610
The best thing to do in a gloomy 
place like this is leave.

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:49.340
<i>This city, the three of 
them, my own history...</i>

00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:51.260
<i>There's something more to it all.</i>

00:14:56.410 --> 00:15:00.860
Oh, my! Will found a fine spear 
like this beneath the ruined city?

00:15:00.860 --> 00:15:04.250
Yeah. The steel is so vivid and 
bright, it absolutely shines.

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:06.490
It's a good, sharp blade.

00:15:06.490 --> 00:15:10.480
It's a short spear made with functionality 
in mind. Truly the work of dwarfs.

00:15:10.480 --> 00:15:13.950
It appears to have several 
Words engraved in it.

00:15:13.950 --> 00:15:16.080
It will be perfect for 
our lesson on appraisal.

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:17.560
Yeah. Teach me all about it.

00:15:19.120 --> 00:15:23.340
<i>Gus hasn't brought up that 
incident at all since then.</i>

00:15:23.930 --> 00:15:27.760
<i>There must be a reason why 
he won't talk about it.</i>

00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:31.350
<i>That's why I decided not 
to tell Blood or Mary.</i>

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:34.670
<i>Later, I appraised the spear with Gus,</i>

00:15:34.670 --> 00:15:37.520
<i>and we found that it had 
the name "Pale Moon."</i>

00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:41.490
<i>Words of Creation are engraved on 
both the spearhead and the shaft.</i>

00:15:41.490 --> 00:15:44.090
<i>The spearhead can emit light magic,</i>

00:15:44.090 --> 00:15:46.160
<i>so it can serve as a light 
source or distract enemies.</i>

00:15:46.550 --> 00:15:48.790
<i>The shaft is imbued with 
magic that allows one</i>

00:15:48.790 --> 00:15:51.770
<i>to expand or shorten the spear at will.</i>

00:15:52.160 --> 00:15:53.950
<i>That should make it easy to carry.</i>

00:15:55.230 --> 00:15:56.260
<i>Above all,</i>

00:15:56.260 --> 00:16:00.010
<i>I was excited to have a magic 
weapon of my very own.</i>

00:16:04.330 --> 00:16:08.840
<i>After that, I returned to the city underground 
every now and then for Blood's lessons.</i>

00:16:09.270 --> 00:16:11.280
<i>I head underground with only a short sword</i>

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:14.170
<i>to collect any weapons 
and armor that I found.</i>

00:16:14.170 --> 00:16:15.960
<i>It was tough at first,</i>

00:16:15.960 --> 00:16:18.230
<i>but I can handle it without any trouble now.</i>

00:16:20.070 --> 00:16:22.780
<i>Even if I encounter Vraskus 
or similarly strong enemy,</i>

00:16:22.780 --> 00:16:24.290
<i>I don't struggle anymore.</i>

00:16:25.910 --> 00:16:26.800
Huh?

00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:28.380
This is it?

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:31.370
You have acquired more 
than enough knowledge.

00:16:31.370 --> 00:16:34.230
It is time for you to learn something else.

00:16:34.230 --> 00:16:35.440
Something else?

00:16:35.440 --> 00:16:39.150
You will enter the city 
underground and collect coins.

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:42.530
I'm going to teach you 
something very important.

00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:45.320
Is this enough?

00:16:45.320 --> 00:16:47.350
Yes, it will do.

00:16:47.350 --> 00:16:49.270
Hey, you finally gonna 
do that again, old man?

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:53.960
Um, Gus?

00:16:53.960 --> 00:16:54.780
Yes?

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:57.160
Isn't this what they call... gambling?

00:16:57.160 --> 00:16:59.130
What a vulgar way to describe it!

00:16:59.130 --> 00:17:01.300
Call it something refined, 
like a game of intellect.

00:17:01.300 --> 00:17:02.410
It's gambling!

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:06.200
Come on! I was all excited when you said 
you'd teach me something important!

00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:08.370
Now, now, don't get angry.

00:17:08.640 --> 00:17:12.010
Besides, games such as these 
should not be underestimated.

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:15.220
They are often used in 
duels between sorcerers.

00:17:15.420 --> 00:17:17.340
Do I really have to place a bet, though?

00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:19.700
Where's the fun in it if you don't?

00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:22.400
I get it. You're scared, aren't you?

00:17:22.400 --> 00:17:23.270
Huh?!

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:25.770
Yes, you should flee.

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:31.080
You very well should be scared to compete 
against the one hailed as the Wandering Sage.

00:17:31.370 --> 00:17:32.770
How dare you?!

00:17:34.290 --> 00:17:35.280
Two sixes!

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:37.480
Yeah! I win!

00:17:37.900 --> 00:17:41.140
Your competitive intuition 
never fails to astound me...

00:17:41.140 --> 00:17:43.230
Once more! I've got it this time!

00:17:45.050 --> 00:17:47.840
What are you two teaching Will?

00:17:47.840 --> 00:17:48.950
Ah, er...

00:17:48.950 --> 00:17:50.170
Mary, there's a reason for—

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:51.300
It was Gus!

00:17:51.900 --> 00:17:55.130
All three of you, sit down right there.

00:17:56.210 --> 00:17:59.750
<i>Mary's lecture was long and scathing.</i>

00:17:59.750 --> 00:18:01.920
<i>I learned something very important.</i>

00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:05.580
<i>It's not good to get hooked on gambling.</i>

00:18:08.800 --> 00:18:09.960
Will.

00:18:10.930 --> 00:18:15.390
I have been observing the heavens for the 
past several years to pass the time,

00:18:15.390 --> 00:18:17.700
so I know when the winter solstice is.

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:20.420
That will be the day you turn fifteen

00:18:20.420 --> 00:18:22.210
and undergo your coming-of-age ritual.

00:18:22.570 --> 00:18:23.310
Yeah.

00:18:23.630 --> 00:18:27.460
I believe that, shortly before 
your coming-of-age ritual,

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:33.060
Blood will challenge you to a one-on-one 
swordfight, an earnest duel.

00:18:33.060 --> 00:18:35.000
I get that feeling, too.

00:18:35.660 --> 00:18:38.460
I know it won't be easy, 
but I'll do my best to win.

00:18:38.780 --> 00:18:41.920
I can't make the three of you 
feel at ease if I don't.

00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:46.910
I would like you to do something for me.

00:18:46.910 --> 00:18:47.630
Sure.

00:18:48.110 --> 00:18:53.730
Could you find a way to lose the duel 
in a way that Blood won't notice?

00:18:55.410 --> 00:18:56.580
Why?

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:58.000
I need you to.

00:18:58.000 --> 00:18:59.750
No, not that!

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:02.740
I'm asking why you're always 
leaving me out of the loop!

00:19:03.210 --> 00:19:08.550
I know you would never trample on 
someone's feelings without a reason!

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:12.890
Didn't I tell you before that I trust you?

00:19:12.890 --> 00:19:16.900
If you'd just explain your reasons, 
I'd be glad to throw the duel!

00:19:16.900 --> 00:19:19.160
I'd even risk my life, 
just like that last time...

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:21.790
So why won't you tell me anything?!

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:24.440
Don't you trust me at all?!

00:19:24.440 --> 00:19:28.380
Am I just that useless to you?!

00:19:29.610 --> 00:19:32.430
Forgive me. I cannot explain.

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:34.300
I see.

00:19:34.680 --> 00:19:36.730
Well, then, I can't help you.

00:19:37.030 --> 00:19:40.060
I'll pretend I didn't hear a 
word of what you just said.

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:52.080
In your coming-of-age ritual, you will 
need to swear an oath to one of the gods

00:19:52.080 --> 00:19:54.800
and decide which one will 
be your guardian deity.

00:19:55.830 --> 00:19:56.680
Will?

00:19:56.680 --> 00:19:57.850
Something wrong?

00:19:58.250 --> 00:19:59.710
No, nothing.

00:19:59.710 --> 00:20:02.220
Anyway, which of the gods do you recommend?

00:20:02.220 --> 00:20:04.680
The one that is the most widely followed

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:07.740
is the god of justice and order, 
the lightning god Volt.

00:20:07.980 --> 00:20:10.220
But you worship the earth-mother Mater,

00:20:10.220 --> 00:20:12.670
Blood worships Blaze, 
the god of fire and smithing,

00:20:12.670 --> 00:20:14.850
and Gus worships the wind god Whirl, right?

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:18.150
Yeah, and what you swear 
to them is important.

00:20:18.430 --> 00:20:22.360
I swore to Blaze that I would 
train every day and grow strong.

00:20:22.550 --> 00:20:27.050
I swore to Mater that I would live 
in a way that would honor her will.

00:20:27.050 --> 00:20:28.210
And Gus?

00:20:28.520 --> 00:20:30.900
There is a god of knowledge,

00:20:30.900 --> 00:20:36.580
but he says he swore to the wind god that 
he would do as he pleased and enjoy life.

00:20:36.580 --> 00:20:39.680
He hates being bound by anything, after all.

00:20:40.930 --> 00:20:43.550
I wonder if he's really enjoying life.

00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:47.670
Sometimes being very smart also 
makes you very transparent.

00:20:47.670 --> 00:20:50.180
That goes for both you and Gus.

00:20:50.400 --> 00:20:54.690
When you swear an oath to a god, 
you earn some divine protection, right?

00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:58.060
Yeah. The stronger your vow, 
the easier it is to earn it.

00:20:58.060 --> 00:21:02.770
But they also say that you'll be destined 
to suffer many hardships in exchange.

00:21:02.770 --> 00:21:05.950
So don't swear your oath 
in the heat of a moment.

00:21:06.310 --> 00:21:09.720
As they say, either you 
become a hero or you die.

00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:12.450
An oath, huh?

00:22:45.180 --> 00:22:48.770
You'll probably start 
growing facial hair soon.

00:22:48.770 --> 00:22:51.750
Maybe I should have Blood 
teach me how to shave.

00:22:52.520 --> 00:22:55.690
I don't think he's shaved in 
a very long time himself.

00:22:55.960 --> 00:22:59.660
Hey... What did Blood look like before?

00:22:59.660 --> 00:23:02.840
It was very different from you.

00:23:02.840 --> 00:23:06.120
He had a thick neck and 
thick arms, broad shoulders,

00:23:06.340 --> 00:23:08.800
a mane like a lion's, and keen eyes.

00:23:08.800 --> 00:23:11.240
He might have looked a bit scary, in fact.

00:23:11.240 --> 00:23:12.840
I can kind of picture it.

00:23:13.620 --> 00:23:15.740
He was quite dashing.

00:23:16.190 --> 00:23:17.940
There, all done.

00:23:17.940 --> 00:23:19.980
I think you look very handsome.

00:23:20.490 --> 00:23:23.380
I wish I looked more like Blood.

00:23:23.380 --> 00:23:27.130
A strong, intimidating face seems 
like it would be more useful.

00:23:27.500 --> 00:23:29.750
Come the next winter solstice, 
you will be an adult.

00:23:30.530 --> 00:23:34.060
Your face has truly begun 
to look like that of a man.

00:23:35.510 --> 00:23:39.970
Episode 3
Payday
